WEBVTT

1
00:00:31.056 --> 00:00:39.055
<font color="#ffff80"><b>Fixed & Synced by bozxphd. Enjoy The Flick</b>.</font>

2
00:00:39.456 --> 00:00:42.125
<i>For as long as humans
have existed on earth,</i>

3
00:00:42.668 --> 00:00:44.586
<i>we have looked to the heavens in wonder.</i>

4
00:00:46.505 --> 00:00:49.841
<i>Fascinated by the countless stars
in the night sky.</i>

5
00:01:03.355 --> 00:01:06.567
<i>But in all the unimaginable
vastness of space,</i>

6
00:01:08.485 --> 00:01:10.696
<i>we found only one place like this.</i>

7
00:01:17.369 --> 00:01:20.956
<i>It's a small blue planet,
with a rocky moon.</i>

8
00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:23.458
<i>Travelling around a star.</i>

9
00:01:34.803 --> 00:01:37.514
<i>It's just close enough
to be fed by its sun's energy,</i>

10
00:01:39.308 --> 00:01:40.976
<i>but not blasted by its heat.</i>

11
00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:47.274
<i>It spins on its axis,</i>

12
00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.902
<i>so that for half a day
its surface basks in light,</i>

13
00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:54.781
<i>then for half it cools in shade.</i>

14
00:02:08.337 --> 00:02:10.756
<i>You might say, it's the lucky planet.</i>

15
00:02:12.215 --> 00:02:14.176
<i>Because its rhythm of light and shade,</i>

16
00:02:14.635 --> 00:02:18.555
<i>turns out to be a vital ingredient,
for life itself.</i>

17
00:02:52.589 --> 00:02:54.883
<i>Earth, our home.</i>

18
00:02:56.468 --> 00:02:59.846
<i>As far as we know, our planet is unique.</i>

19
00:03:01.098 --> 00:03:02.432
<i>As far as we know,</i>

20
00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:08.021
<i>one day spent here is the most
amazing thing in the whole universe.</i>

21
00:03:43.682 --> 00:03:45.851
<i>The magical dance of earth and sun,</i>

22
00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:49.271
<i>has created millions of different kinds
of plants and animals,</i>

23
00:03:49.354 --> 00:03:51.565
<i>alive on our earth today.</i>

24
00:03:56.278 --> 00:03:57.571
<i>Some, you see every day.</i>

25
00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.950
<i>Others, are very rare.</i>

26
00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.168
<i>But, we all have one thing in common.</i>

27
00:04:14.838 --> 00:04:18.842
<i>Our lives are driven
by the rhythm of night and day.</i>

28
00:04:22.763 --> 00:04:24.765
One <i>hint of morning sunlight...</i>

29
00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:28.185
<i>And we respond in so many different ways.</i>

30
00:05:04.054 --> 00:05:05.263
<i>Some animals need it.</i>

31
00:05:08.725 --> 00:05:10.310
<i>Others, hide from it.</i>

32
00:05:14.231 --> 00:05:15.941
<i>Most of us, love it.</i>

33
00:05:24.533 --> 00:05:26.701
<i>Some, even greet it with song.</i>

34
00:06:17.419 --> 00:06:19.087
<i>Whatever way we choose to meet it,</i>

35
00:06:21.172 --> 00:06:24.676
<i>sunrise is the power
that brings our world to life.</i>

36
00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:36.313
<i>Africa.</i>

37
00:06:38.773 --> 00:06:43.069
<i>Here, the first hours of the day belong
not just to those who rise early,</i>

38
00:06:44.446 --> 00:06:46.114
<i>but to those who stayed up late.</i>

39
00:07:20.857 --> 00:07:22.776
<i>This serval has been hunting
during the night.</i>

40
00:07:26.363 --> 00:07:28.198
<i>But now he's pushing his luck.</i>

41
00:07:29.699 --> 00:07:32.702
<i>He's out late,
trying for a final mouthful.</i>

42
00:07:40.418 --> 00:07:42.170
<i>His high jumping technique is perfect,</i>

43
00:07:42.253 --> 00:07:45.632
<i>for hunting amongst the long grass
of the African Savanna.</i>

44
00:07:48.802 --> 00:07:53.223
<i>He's looking for prey,
but mostly listening for it.</i>

45
00:07:57.769 --> 00:08:00.814
<i>His enormous radar ears
can hear a pin drop.</i>

46
00:08:07.862 --> 00:08:10.865
<i>Or a careless step
from a Southern vlei rat.</i>

47
00:08:34.848 --> 00:08:38.226
<i>Now the sunlight's growing stronger,
maybe it's time for bed.</i>

48
00:08:53.283 --> 00:08:58.329
<i>On the other side of the world,
on an isolated group of pacific islands,</i>

49
00:09:00.665 --> 00:09:04.961
<i>there are animals who can't even think
about running around so early in the day.</i>

50
00:09:09.841 --> 00:09:14.345
<i>They can't do anything until they've
been warmed up by the sun's power.</i>

51
00:09:24.522 --> 00:09:28.902
<i>The galapagos islands are home for some
of the most unusual animals on earth.</i>

52
00:09:31.446 --> 00:09:32.614
<i>Marine iguana.</i>

53
00:09:40.205 --> 00:09:42.499
<i>Their morning ritual is always the same.</i>

54
00:09:43.833 --> 00:09:46.377
<i>As the sun comes up on their island home,</i>

55
00:09:47.295 --> 00:09:49.672
<i>they simply sprawl on the rocks,</i>

56
00:09:50.507 --> 00:09:51.424
<i>lapping it up.</i>

57
00:10:02.018 --> 00:10:04.187
<i>Reptiles are pretty much solar-powered.</i>

58
00:10:05.855 --> 00:10:08.650
<i>They need the sun's heat,
before they can move a muscle.</i>

59
00:10:27.627 --> 00:10:30.046
<i>And they're not the only creatures
soaking up the sun.</i>

60
00:10:38.721 --> 00:10:42.934
<i>Galapagos racer snakes aren't big enough
to trouble an adult iguana.</i>

61
00:10:44.727 --> 00:10:46.813
<i>But, something smaller?</i>

62
00:10:58.658 --> 00:11:02.912
<i>Away from the rocks where grown-ups live,
buried in the sand,</i>

63
00:11:03.746 --> 00:11:05.957
<i>baby iguanas have been incubating
underground...</i>

64
00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.251
<i>For over three months.</i>

65
00:11:11.296 --> 00:11:13.715
<i>Today when the sun has warmed the sand,</i>

66
00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:16.759
<i>they will emerge.</i>

67
00:11:27.437 --> 00:11:31.608
<i>It's time for this one,
to crawl out into the rest of life.</i>

68
00:11:34.903 --> 00:11:37.947
<i>If she starts too early,
before she's warm enough,</i>

69
00:11:39.157 --> 00:11:41.576
<i>she won't have the energy
to run very fast.</i>

70
00:11:45.955 --> 00:11:50.251
<i>If she leaves too late,
then her enemies may be supercharged.</i>

71
00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:54.255
<i>It's the biggest decision
she'll ever make.</i>

72
00:12:39.884 --> 00:12:40.885
<i>She made it.</i>

73
00:12:42.553 --> 00:12:44.222
<i>The snakes missed their chance.</i>

74
00:12:51.813 --> 00:12:53.481
<i>But more babies are hatching.</i>

75
00:12:55.358 --> 00:12:57.402
<i>And now the snakes are on alert.</i>

76
00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:04.951
<i>It's the best opportunity
they will get to eat all year.</i>

77
00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:33.396
<i>On flat ground a baby iguana
can outrun a racer snake.</i>

78
00:13:35.315 --> 00:13:38.735
<i>But, others are waiting in ambush.</i>

79
00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:12.101
<i>Another hatchling has his first glimpse
of a dangerous world.</i>

80
00:15:09.659 --> 00:15:11.411
<i>The snake's eyes aren't very good,</i>

81
00:15:13.079 --> 00:15:14.831
<i>but they can detect movement.</i>

82
00:15:19.836 --> 00:15:23.923
<i>So, if the hatchling keeps its nerve,
it may just be okay.</i>

83
00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:33.993
<i>An amazing escape.</i>

84
00:16:35.703 --> 00:16:38.498
<i>The biggest achievement
of any young animal's life.</i>

85
00:16:39.749 --> 00:16:42.126
<i>Powered by our local star.</i>

86
00:16:55.723 --> 00:16:56.724
<i>Mid-morning.</i>

87
00:16:58.851 --> 00:17:02.313
<i>As the sun climbs higher,
its rays reach further.</i>

88
00:17:04.607 --> 00:17:06.943
<i>Bringing magic wherever they touch.</i>

89
00:17:28.798 --> 00:17:31.133
<i>Plants turn the light into life.</i>

90
00:17:34.053 --> 00:17:40.101
<i>They take thin air and the sun's energy
and with photosynthesis make new growth.</i>

91
00:17:41.852 --> 00:17:47.483
<i>Conjuring up tangled forest worlds,
leaf by leaf.</i>

92
00:18:09.589 --> 00:18:12.758
<i>It's the alchemy upon which
everything else on earth depends.</i>

93
00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:15.469
<i>A matter of life,</i>

94
00:18:17.138 --> 00:18:18.055
<i>and death.</i>

95
00:18:43.205 --> 00:18:46.667
<i>One plant can weave
its particular spell in a single Clay.</i>

96
00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:54.091
<i>This is bamboo.</i>

97
00:18:55.259 --> 00:18:57.470
<i>It can grow almost a millimetre a minute.</i>

98
00:18:58.929 --> 00:19:01.015
<i>The fastest growing plant in the world.</i>

99
00:19:14.028 --> 00:19:15.446
<i>It's still only mid-morning.</i>

100
00:19:16.447 --> 00:19:18.824
<i>Most of this has grown since dawn.</i>

101
00:19:28.459 --> 00:19:32.922
<i>And since dawn,
this giant panda has been eating it.</i>

102
00:19:38.344 --> 00:19:42.223
<i>The trouble with bamboo,
is that it's not very nutritious.</i>

103
00:19:45.059 --> 00:19:47.395
<i>The trouble with pandas,
is that they're very fussy.</i>

104
00:19:50.064 --> 00:19:52.191
<i>Bamboo is almost
the only thing they'll eat.</i>

105
00:19:58.114 --> 00:20:00.157
<i>To get enough energy to feed herself,</i>

106
00:20:00.449 --> 00:20:03.577
<i>this panda will need
to eat up to 14 hours today.</i>

107
00:20:05.579 --> 00:20:08.290
<i>Longer probably, because she's nursing.</i>

108
00:20:12.044 --> 00:20:14.130
<i>But for her cub, it's different.</i>

109
00:20:16.382 --> 00:20:21.929
<i>She lives mostly on her mother's milk,
so chewing is only really her hobby.</i>

110
00:20:24.056 --> 00:20:25.641
<i>Not yet a full-time job.</i>

111
00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:58.048
<i>This morning, she has something
rare in the natural world.</i>

112
00:21:00.968 --> 00:21:02.052
<i>Time to spare.</i>

113
00:21:04.263 --> 00:21:06.015
<i>And, to explore.</i>

114
00:21:54.146 --> 00:21:56.607
<i>Because of their specialised way of life,</i>

115
00:21:57.775 --> 00:22:01.111
<i>giant pandas are amongst
the rarest animals in the world.</i>

116
00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:07.076
<i>Cubs like her are more precious still.</i>

117
00:22:08.536 --> 00:22:10.538
<i>There are only a few hundred alive.</i>

118
00:22:17.127 --> 00:22:20.673
<i>A rare animal with the rarest luxury.</i>

119
00:22:23.217 --> 00:22:24.134
<i>Time.</i>

120
00:22:46.699 --> 00:22:48.742
<i>As the morning sun grows in strength,</i>

121
00:22:50.244 --> 00:22:52.746
<i>it begins to brew a spell
of a different kind.</i>

122
00:22:56.792 --> 00:23:01.755
<i>The sun is pouring energy
into our atmosphere, heating it up.</i>

123
00:23:05.759 --> 00:23:08.095
<i>It evaporates water from land and sea,</i>

124
00:23:10.014 --> 00:23:11.891
<i>and builds clouds.</i>

125
00:23:38.167 --> 00:23:42.129
<i>Across Africa, clouds and weather
are constantly on the move,</i>

126
00:23:43.756 --> 00:23:49.178
<i>bringing rain and fresh grass
to different places at different times.</i>

127
00:23:52.848 --> 00:23:56.852
<i>For millions of animals,
the job of every morning is to move</i>

128
00:24:00.147 --> 00:24:02.566
<i>to where the rain
will make the grass grow next.</i>

129
00:24:03.567 --> 00:24:05.361
<i>Whatever stands in their way.</i>

130
00:24:13.285 --> 00:24:14.495
<i>This morning,</i>

131
00:24:14.578 --> 00:24:19.166
<i>the need to keep moving will present a
particular challenge for one young zebra.</i>

132
00:24:25.089 --> 00:24:28.133
<i>This foal could walk
less than an hour after birth.</i>

133
00:24:32.054 --> 00:24:33.597
<i>She can handle almost anything.</i>

134
00:24:44.358 --> 00:24:47.486
<i>But she's never faced
an obstacle like this.</i>

135
00:24:52.032 --> 00:24:56.704
<i>Swollen by highland rain,
the river is fast and furious.</i>

136
00:25:00.958 --> 00:25:02.376
<i>And full of dangers.</i>

137
00:25:34.074 --> 00:25:37.286
<i>The young zebra is going to need
every bit of her mother's help,</i>

138
00:25:37.578 --> 00:25:39.079
<i>if she's going to make it.</i>

139
00:26:51.318 --> 00:26:54.822
<i>It turns out the biggest threat
isn't attack by other animals,</i>

140
00:26:55.697 --> 00:26:57.157
<i>it's the river itself.</i>

141
00:27:03.330 --> 00:27:06.583
<i>Her mother tries to lead the foal
to the shallowest waters,</i>

142
00:27:07.835 --> 00:27:09.586
<i>but she's just too small.</i>

143
00:27:12.965 --> 00:27:14.883
<i>And the current's just too strong.</i>

144
00:27:24.852 --> 00:27:27.563
<i>The foal is on the verge of exhaustion,</i>

145
00:27:29.231 --> 00:27:30.983
<i>but her mother will not give up.</i>

146
00:27:53.213 --> 00:27:57.885
<i>While others are escaping,
she calls for her foal to keep going.</i>

147
00:28:18.906 --> 00:28:21.617
<i>And finally, a way out.</i>

148
00:28:30.542 --> 00:28:35.589
<i>There is a saying in Africa,
"lf you wanna go quickly, go alone.</i>

149
00:28:36.590 --> 00:28:39.593
<i>If you wanna go far, go together."</i>

150
00:28:54.024 --> 00:28:54.900
<i>After this,</i>

151
00:28:54.983 --> 00:28:59.905
<i>the zebra foal and her mother can surely
handle anything the day throws at them.</i>

152
00:29:10.207 --> 00:29:13.210
<i>The sun is approaching
its highest and most powerful.</i>

153
00:29:21.927 --> 00:29:24.346
<i>In the far north, in the arctic,</i>

154
00:29:25.472 --> 00:29:28.809
<i>ice has held land and ocean
in its grip for months.</i>

155
00:29:31.103 --> 00:29:34.564
<i>The sun near the poles is always lower
and weaker than anywhere else.</i>

156
00:29:36.275 --> 00:29:39.194
<i>But still, its energy will transform.</i>

157
00:29:54.626 --> 00:29:55.627
<i>Narwhal.</i>

158
00:30:00.340 --> 00:30:02.968
<i>One of the most mysterious
animals on the planet.</i>

159
00:30:12.519 --> 00:30:14.604
<i>For the moment they can't travel far,</i>

160
00:30:17.232 --> 00:30:20.861
<i>only small openings in the ice
allow them to surface and breathe.</i>

161
00:30:24.281 --> 00:30:27.326
<i>But the power of the sun
is coming to their rescue.</i>

162
00:30:38.879 --> 00:30:39.796
<i>For many days</i>

163
00:30:39.880 --> 00:30:43.759
<i>the sun's heat has been gnawing away
at the ice's hold on sea and land.</i>

164
00:30:50.140 --> 00:30:55.312
<i>Now, approaching its highest
and strongest, the sun begins to triumph.</i>

165
00:30:57.647 --> 00:31:01.985
<i>And the battle of heat against cold,
becomes a rout.</i>

166
00:32:12.055 --> 00:32:15.100
<i>On land, rivers flow again.</i>

167
00:32:19.896 --> 00:32:22.691
<i>In the oceans, where the ice is now weak,</i>

168
00:32:25.610 --> 00:32:27.904
<i>the sun's warmth, opens cracks.</i>

169
00:32:32.701 --> 00:32:34.995
<i>And the cracks become channels.</i>

170
00:32:37.164 --> 00:32:40.834
<i>Roadways along, which the narwhal
can traverse their icy kingdom.</i>

171
00:32:46.256 --> 00:32:50.010
<i>In inuit legend, the first narwhal
was a brave female hunter.</i>

172
00:32:52.721 --> 00:32:55.599
<i>Caught up in a deadly embrace
with a whale she hunted,</i>

173
00:32:59.144 --> 00:33:02.772
<i>her braided hair flung out,
becoming the twisted tusk.</i>

174
00:33:29.591 --> 00:33:32.636
<i>For these narwhal, what an amazing day.</i>

175
00:33:34.888 --> 00:33:38.475
<i>They are free again,
to roam their ocean home.</i>

176
00:33:52.906 --> 00:33:57.244
<i>The strength of the sun becomes greater
and greater, the further south you go.</i>

177
00:34:07.879 --> 00:34:09.548
<i>In the mountains of north America,</i>

178
00:34:10.131 --> 00:34:14.678
<i>the sunlight of a spring day,
brings the freshly thawed world to life.</i>

179
00:34:29.568 --> 00:34:31.820
<i>If you're still wearing your winter coat,</i>

180
00:34:32.320 --> 00:34:35.115
<i>the heat during the middle-of-the-day
can get a bit uncomfortable.</i>

181
00:34:38.785 --> 00:34:42.914
<i>You need to find a tree
and give yourself a good scratch.</i>

182
00:35:07.939 --> 00:35:11.026
<i>Rubbing against the bark
not only gets to the itch,</i>

183
00:35:11.735 --> 00:35:14.154
<i>it helps a hot bear shed its winter fur.</i>

184
00:35:19.075 --> 00:35:22.746
<i>It's also a chance to mark the territory
with your personal scent.</i>

185
00:35:24.414 --> 00:35:26.958
<i>So everyone knows exactly who's in town.</i>

186
00:36:26.685 --> 00:36:28.269
<i>It's now midday,</i>

187
00:36:28.978 --> 00:36:33.066
<i>and the world feels the full force
of our friendly neighbourhood star.</i>

188
00:36:35.694 --> 00:36:38.405
<i>The sun is now at its highest in the sky.</i>

189
00:36:39.322 --> 00:36:43.284
<i>Its light penetrates even
the deep hidden folds of the earth.</i>

190
00:37:05.432 --> 00:37:11.354
<i>In Africa, near the equator,
its energy creates a furnace.</i>

191
00:37:25.326 --> 00:37:28.663
<i>This zebra foal and her herd
still need to move on.</i>

192
00:37:37.922 --> 00:37:40.550
<i>But every step is tough in heat like this.</i>

193
00:37:48.808 --> 00:37:50.101
<i>Any scrap of shade...</i>

194
00:37:50.852 --> 00:37:51.936
<i>Is an oasis.</i>

195
00:38:07.243 --> 00:38:10.330
<i>In full sunlight,
the herd are easy for hunters to see.</i>

196
00:38:26.387 --> 00:38:28.681
<i>But there is one blessing
about the midday sun.</i>

197
00:38:37.565 --> 00:38:40.235
<i>It's simply too hot for lions to hunt.</i>

198
00:39:07.303 --> 00:39:10.265
<i>There is something, however,
that doesn't take a break,</i>

199
00:39:11.140 --> 00:39:12.809
<i>even in the heat of the day.</i>

200
00:39:15.353 --> 00:39:16.813
<i>The struggle for power.</i>

201
00:39:36.040 --> 00:39:40.962
<i>Rivalry between males for territory
and for the attentions of females</i>

202
00:39:42.130 --> 00:39:46.509
<i>is so overpowering, it drives even
the most placid of creatures to combat.</i>

203
00:39:51.764 --> 00:39:53.641
<i>At high noon in the desert heat,</i>

204
00:39:56.686 --> 00:40:01.399
a <i>young male giraffe is challenging
the resident bull for prime territory</i>

205
00:40:02.108 --> 00:40:03.985
<i>and the females that go with it.</i>

206
00:40:26.883 --> 00:40:30.345
<i>At first they just push and shove,
trying to intimidate each other.</i>

207
00:40:32.597 --> 00:40:34.515
<i>Normally, this would be an end to it,</i>

208
00:40:36.017 --> 00:40:40.563
<i>but the young rival seems to think
he has a chance and attacks.</i>

209
00:41:22.397 --> 00:41:23.690
<i>Neither will back down.</i>

210
00:41:47.672 --> 00:41:49.132
<i>The old bull is down.</i>

211
00:41:52.010 --> 00:41:53.928
<i>He knows the final blow is coming.</i>

212
00:41:57.390 --> 00:41:58.683
<i>So, he ducks...</i>

213
00:42:00.935 --> 00:42:02.103
<i>And hits back.</i>

214
00:42:27.879 --> 00:42:28.796
<i>It is over.</i>

215
00:42:37.305 --> 00:42:39.807
<i>The day still belongs to the old master.</i>

216
00:42:43.394 --> 00:42:46.647
<i>For the loser, it's exile in the desert.</i>

217
00:43:29.398 --> 00:43:34.320
<i>The land and the creatures that live
on it, toast under the noonday sun.</i>

218
00:43:41.119 --> 00:43:45.206
<i>But one habitat remains cool, even now.</i>

219
00:43:55.508 --> 00:43:59.720
<i>Over the course of a single day,
even the enormous power of the sun,</i>

220
00:43:59.804 --> 00:44:03.224
<i>isn't strong enough to warm
the great oceans by much.</i>

221
00:44:06.602 --> 00:44:09.230
<i>Here, some of the largest
creatures on earth,</i>

222
00:44:09.730 --> 00:44:13.109
<i>live lives as long,
and perhaps as complex, as our own.</i>

223
00:44:29.750 --> 00:44:32.378
<i>This is a family of sperm whales.</i>

224
00:44:42.221 --> 00:44:44.849
<i>And at its heart, a rare sight.</i>

225
00:44:46.559 --> 00:44:47.476
<i>A calf.</i>

226
00:44:51.230 --> 00:44:54.317
<i>Already 15ft long, she's about a year old,</i>

227
00:44:56.527 --> 00:44:58.070
<i>and very inquisitive.</i>

228
00:45:19.592 --> 00:45:22.637
<i>For two or three years,
she will feed on her mother's milk.</i>

229
00:45:23.471 --> 00:45:27.266
<i>It's so rich in fat,
it has the consistency of cottage cheese.</i>

230
00:45:28.059 --> 00:45:31.354
<i>So it doesn't dissolve in the sea
water as it's being gulped down.</i>

231
00:45:41.572 --> 00:45:45.159
<i>The great whales are the biggest
predators that have ever existed,</i>

232
00:45:46.369 --> 00:45:49.038
<i>yet, they make
the most protective parents.</i>

233
00:45:53.668 --> 00:45:54.961
<i>And very talkative ones,</i>

234
00:45:56.003 --> 00:45:58.089
<i>chatting in a language of clicks.</i>

235
00:46:01.217 --> 00:46:03.094
<i>They're the loudest
creatures on the planet,</i>

236
00:46:03.928 --> 00:46:06.847
<i>capable of sounds,
far louder than a jet engine.</i>

237
00:46:16.190 --> 00:46:18.818
<i>But right now, it's time for silence.</i>

238
00:46:22.405 --> 00:46:24.407
<i>Hanging vertically,
the giants of the sea...</i>

239
00:46:25.449 --> 00:46:26.742
<i>Take an afternoon nap.</i>

240
00:46:41.257 --> 00:46:44.427
<i>These whales have brains larger
than any other animal.</i>

241
00:46:49.932 --> 00:46:53.644
<i>Who can guess with what richness
they dream away the day.</i>

242
00:47:51.243 --> 00:47:56.457
<i>In the tropics, the oppressive heat
of midday lingers well into the afternoon.</i>

243
00:47:59.919 --> 00:48:03.547
<i>On a tiny island, off the coast of Panama,
in central America,</i>

244
00:48:05.007 --> 00:48:07.176
<i>everything takes life slowly.</i>

245
00:48:18.145 --> 00:48:20.231
<i>A pygmy three-toed sloth.</i>

246
00:48:24.527 --> 00:48:27.988
<i>At his best, he is slothful.</i>

247
00:48:35.371 --> 00:48:37.623
<i>At this time of day,
he's pretty much comatose.</i>

248
00:48:50.845 --> 00:48:52.888
<i>Only one thing might rouse him.</i>

249
00:48:57.351 --> 00:48:58.185
<i>And it's this...</i>

250
00:49:01.063 --> 00:49:05.901
<i>The call of the female sloth,
out there somewhere.</i>

251
00:49:12.032 --> 00:49:14.785
<i>And since it's high tide,
why not take the short cut.</i>

252
00:49:25.963 --> 00:49:28.632
<i>The only problem is from down here,</i>

253
00:49:29.467 --> 00:49:33.220
<i>it's not easy to tell where
the potential mate is calling from.</i>

254
00:50:09.632 --> 00:50:10.633
<i>Could this be her?</i>

255
00:50:59.390 --> 00:51:02.935
<i>Sadly for him,
this female is not looking for a date.</i>

256
00:51:11.151 --> 00:51:14.780
<i>While she's nursing her cub,
she's quite happy to stay single.</i>

257
00:51:21.912 --> 00:51:26.041
<i>As they say, “mafiana.“
there's always tomorrow.</i>

258
00:51:48.355 --> 00:51:50.899
<i>Though island life here moves slowly,</i>

259
00:51:51.984 --> 00:51:55.696
<i>the pace of the afternoon is very
different in other parts of the world.</i>

260
00:52:25.267 --> 00:52:28.187
<i>This is zavodovski island in Antarctica,</i>

261
00:52:28.729 --> 00:52:32.066
<i>home for 1.5 million chinstrap penguins.</i>

262
00:52:47.373 --> 00:52:49.083
<i>It's an extraordinary place.</i>

263
00:52:49.667 --> 00:52:53.712
<i>An outcrop of rock,
spewed out by the volcano at its heart.</i>

264
00:53:00.219 --> 00:53:02.805
<i>The oceans beat against it night and day.</i>

265
00:53:10.396 --> 00:53:13.023
<i>And the penguins
are caught in the crossfire.</i>

266
00:53:19.738 --> 00:53:22.282
<i>All day, the adult penguins
struggle against the waves</i>

267
00:53:22.366 --> 00:53:25.369
<i>as they journey between home
and their hunting grounds, offshore.</i>

268
00:53:28.706 --> 00:53:30.457
<i>It's an ordeal they can't avoid.</i>

269
00:53:33.377 --> 00:53:34.795
<i>Their families depend on them.</i>

270
00:53:39.258 --> 00:53:41.719
<i>Chinstrap penguin chicks
are completely helpless,</i>

271
00:53:41.802 --> 00:53:44.430
<i>without the support
of both mother and father.</i>

272
00:53:48.809 --> 00:53:50.644
<i>They need fresh food every day.</i>

273
00:53:53.772 --> 00:53:55.774
<i>And their parents take turns to fetch it.</i>

274
00:53:59.987 --> 00:54:01.655
<i>It means an awful lot of hunting...</i>

275
00:54:04.324 --> 00:54:06.410
<i>...for an awful lot of moms and dads.</i>

276
00:54:10.873 --> 00:54:13.959
<i>This mother has no food
left to feed her chicks.</i>

277
00:54:17.087 --> 00:54:19.256
<i>They now need their father to return,</i>

278
00:54:20.883 --> 00:54:21.800
<i>and soon.</i>

279
00:54:32.895 --> 00:54:33.729
<i>At mid-afternoon,</i>

280
00:54:33.812 --> 00:54:37.941
<i>the first wave of hunters,
who left early this morning, return.</i>

281
00:54:41.320 --> 00:54:43.489
<i>Amongst them is the chick's father.</i>

282
00:54:46.658 --> 00:54:51.705
<i>He's been fishing 50 miles offshore,
but now he's not far away.</i>

283
00:54:57.628 --> 00:55:02.508
<i>If getting safely into the water
was difficult, getting out is even harder.</i>

284
00:55:28.075 --> 00:55:32.120
<i>Tiny claws help them to get whatever
grip he can on the rough water.</i>

285
00:56:02.734 --> 00:56:05.904
<i>The father now has
a two mile walk to his family.</i>

286
00:56:09.116 --> 00:56:11.326
<i>And a stomach loaded
with food, doesn't help.</i>

287
00:56:19.793 --> 00:56:22.212
<i>This is the largest
penguin colony on earth.</i>

288
00:56:27.843 --> 00:56:30.596
<i>But, as he makes the same
journey every other day,</i>

289
00:56:33.223 --> 00:56:35.559
<i>he should be able
to do it with his eyes closed.</i>

290
00:56:39.146 --> 00:56:40.606
<i>At least, most of the time.</i>

291
00:56:44.151 --> 00:56:46.361
<i>Like any commute,
it can get a little congested.</i>

292
00:56:47.362 --> 00:56:51.033
<i>And sometimes, it can be hard
to remember where you parked your kids.</i>

293
00:56:55.996 --> 00:56:59.791
<i>The mother is still waiting,
the chicks are now desperate.</i>

294
00:57:07.424 --> 00:57:11.803
<i>In the midst of all this deafening chorus,
he can recognise her particular cry.</i>

295
00:57:13.889 --> 00:57:15.599
<i>She is, literally, one in a million.</i>

296
00:57:21.688 --> 00:57:25.233
<i>A head Bob, is the penguin's way
of saying, "welcome home."</i>

297
00:57:33.700 --> 00:57:35.410
<i>Both chicks will get a meal.</i>

298
00:57:41.833 --> 00:57:44.628
<i>A happy end to the toughest
commute on earth.</i>

299
00:57:57.724 --> 00:58:00.727
<i>Mid-afternoon
in the rainforests of Ecuador.</i>

300
00:58:02.896 --> 00:58:04.606
<i>The air steams in the heat.</i>

301
00:58:12.906 --> 00:58:17.369
<i>Here, the sun and plants conspire
to create their own unique weather.</i>

302
00:58:20.080 --> 00:58:21.957
<i>And is the same practically every day.</i>

303
00:58:28.422 --> 00:58:31.633
<i>This afternoon,
that's going to help one of its smallest</i>

304
00:58:31.717 --> 00:58:35.512
<i>and most beautiful inhabitants
in a surprising way.</i>

305
00:58:42.310 --> 00:58:45.772
<i>The racket-tailed hummingbird
is about the size of your thumb.</i>

306
00:58:52.946 --> 00:58:55.365
<i>It takes a lot of energy
to look this graceful.</i>

307
00:59:00.662 --> 00:59:04.249
<i>That means it's living
in a perpetual state of near starvation.</i>

308
00:59:09.004 --> 00:59:13.842
<i>In fact, its metabolism is so fast,
it needs to fuel up on nectar,</i>

309
00:59:13.925 --> 00:59:15.761
<i>over a thousand times a day.</i>

310
00:59:23.268 --> 00:59:25.020
<i>It can't stop feeding for a moment.</i>

311
00:59:26.897 --> 00:59:28.857
<i>All day is a race against time.</i>

312
00:59:57.969 --> 01:00:01.431
<i>The racket-tail isn't the only one
hunting for nectar in the forest flowers.</i>

313
01:00:02.808 --> 01:00:05.811
<i>Bees are too,
and they don't like to share.</i>

314
01:00:10.232 --> 01:00:14.069
<i>A single bee sting,
close to the bird's heart, could be fatal.</i>

315
01:00:39.344 --> 01:00:41.763
<i>But time, is on the racket-taips side.</i>

316
01:00:44.182 --> 01:00:45.892
<i>Rain is about to intervene.</i>

317
01:00:49.855 --> 01:00:54.484
<i>The heat of the afternoon sun,
has built massive thunder clouds.</i>

318
01:01:01.241 --> 01:01:04.578
<i>And when they can no longer
hold their burden, they break.</i>

319
01:01:23.305 --> 01:01:26.266
<i>Above the canopy, the rain is torrential.</i>

320
01:01:30.187 --> 01:01:35.775
<i>Under the shelter of layers of leaves,
the deluge is reduced to drips.</i>

321
01:01:45.368 --> 01:01:50.040
<i>A raindrop as big as its head,
may not be much fun for a hummingbird.</i>

322
01:01:57.505 --> 01:01:59.633
<i>But it's altogether too much, for a bee.</i>

323
01:02:33.416 --> 01:02:35.627
<i>The race to eat, continues.</i>

324
01:02:43.593 --> 01:02:48.515
<i>All over the world, tiny creatures
are on a mission to stock up before night.</i>

325
01:02:55.397 --> 01:02:59.192
<i>In a European Meadow, there's a great
deal of food hidden in the plants.</i>

326
01:03:00.944 --> 01:03:02.153
<i>For those who can reach it.</i>

327
01:03:16.459 --> 01:03:18.086
<i>As the day begins to fade,</i>

328
01:03:18.169 --> 01:03:22.048
<i>this tiny harvest mouse,
must gather as much fuel as possible.</i>

329
01:03:40.317 --> 01:03:41.985
<i>Her best chance for a good dinner,</i>

330
01:03:42.068 --> 01:03:45.613
<i>are the seeds and fruit,
at the tips of the tallest stalks.</i>

331
01:03:51.453 --> 01:03:54.873
<i>But, it's the most dangerous part,
of her tiny world.</i>

332
01:04:15.727 --> 01:04:18.355
<i>A barn owl, is a night-time hunter.</i>

333
01:04:28.448 --> 01:04:29.908
<i>But this one has woken early.</i>

334
01:04:31.743 --> 01:04:32.744
<i>And hungry.</i>

335
01:04:53.890 --> 01:04:57.727
<i>The world at ground-level is bewildering
for a mouse used to the high life.</i>

336
01:05:19.582 --> 01:05:23.044
<i>But she can read the pattern
of the stems overhead, like a map.</i>

337
01:05:32.595 --> 01:05:35.682
<i>Which is just as well,
because back home...</i>

338
01:05:37.434 --> 01:05:38.435
<i>She's needed.</i>

339
01:06:14.637 --> 01:06:16.431
<i>The light is dying.</i>

340
01:06:18.308 --> 01:06:20.310
<i>But new life is being born.</i>

341
01:06:36.534 --> 01:06:38.119
<i>A mayfly emerges.</i>

342
01:06:41.498 --> 01:06:43.249
<i>It will live for just this day.</i>

343
01:06:49.631 --> 01:06:52.675
<i>Or less, if it doesn't move fast enough.</i>

344
01:07:10.276 --> 01:07:12.320
<i>When life is as perilous as this...</i>

345
01:07:17.325 --> 01:07:19.410
<i>Nature finds safety in numbers.</i>

346
01:07:23.289 --> 01:07:25.667
<i>This hatch, on the tisza river in Hungary,</i>

347
01:07:26.376 --> 01:07:28.962
<i>is one of the world's
great wildlife spectacles.</i>

348
01:07:36.761 --> 01:07:39.305
<i>Having spent three years
as nymphs in the river,</i>

349
01:07:40.181 --> 01:07:44.143
<i>up to five million of these
remarkable insects emerge together,</i>

350
01:07:45.645 --> 01:07:47.605
<i>on just this stretch of water alone.</i>

351
01:07:55.697 --> 01:07:58.533
<i>They'll never feed.
They don't even have mouths.</i>

352
01:07:59.659 --> 01:08:05.123
<i>Instead, as soon as they hatch,
they begin a vast glittering mating dance.</i>

353
01:08:19.762 --> 01:08:21.931
<i>Every day on earth is amazing.</i>

354
01:08:23.182 --> 01:08:27.812
<i>But surely the mayfly's day,
is one of the most amazing of all.</i>

355
01:08:33.943 --> 01:08:38.531
<i>By nightfall, they will have met,
mated, laid their eggs, and died.</i>

356
01:08:39.741 --> 01:08:42.201
<i>The future entrusted
to the next generation.</i>

357
01:08:50.126 --> 01:08:54.505
<i>Their entire adult life will be spent
in just a few hours of a single day.</i>

358
01:09:15.652 --> 01:09:19.030
<i>Day, is now spinning swiftly,
towards night.</i>

359
01:09:24.035 --> 01:09:26.954
<i>The sun slips, ever lower in the sky.</i>

360
01:09:31.668 --> 01:09:33.378
<i>It is a time of great beauty...</i>

361
01:09:34.837 --> 01:09:36.089
<i>And grave danger.</i>

362
01:09:43.596 --> 01:09:48.726
<i>In the cool evening shadows,
is the best time to be a predator,</i>

363
01:09:50.186 --> 01:09:52.230
<i>and the worst time to be prey.</i>

364
01:10:00.738 --> 01:10:05.451
<i>For a zebra and her foal, this
is the most dangerous time of the day.</i>

365
01:10:50.204 --> 01:10:52.665
<i>A cheetah has his eye on the foal.</i>

366
01:11:52.308 --> 01:11:56.062
<i>- Sometimes</i> a <i>mother's love...</i>

367
01:11:56.145 --> 01:11:57.980
<i>Can be a match for almost anything.</i>

368
01:12:13.454 --> 01:12:17.625
<i>As the day fades,
the shadow world is taking over.</i>

369
01:12:21.295 --> 01:12:23.965
<i>In the changzhou mountains,
in southwest China,</i>

370
01:12:25.091 --> 01:12:28.386
<i>the world is turning its face
away from its nurturing star,</i>

371
01:12:29.470 --> 01:12:31.806
<i>towards the chilly emptiness of space.</i>

372
01:12:37.687 --> 01:12:42.066
<i>Here, white-headed langurs
are taking their last meal of the day.</i>

373
01:12:46.946 --> 01:12:49.156
<i>They're amongst
the rarest creatures on earth.</i>

374
01:12:50.283 --> 01:12:52.326
<i>Rarer, even than the giant panda.</i>

375
01:12:58.124 --> 01:13:03.754
<i>But when daylight disappears,
this is no place to linger.</i>

376
01:13:26.611 --> 01:13:29.739
<i>They are obeying an ancient
and overpowering instinct.</i>

377
01:13:44.420 --> 01:13:49.383
<i>With the lengthening of the shadows,
they scramble for height and refuge.</i>

378
01:13:58.351 --> 01:14:00.144
<i>The route is precarious.</i>

379
01:14:01.187 --> 01:14:03.105
<i>It's not unknown for a langur to fall,</i>

380
01:14:04.607 --> 01:14:06.359
<i>or baby be dropped.</i>

381
01:14:15.409 --> 01:14:19.872
<i>Yet, despite the risks,
the iangurs never stay out after dark.</i>

382
01:14:55.032 --> 01:14:58.327
<i>Even the babies feel it,
and know to fear it.</i>

383
01:15:01.914 --> 01:15:03.165
<i>Night is coming.</i>

384
01:15:05.710 --> 01:15:07.920
<i>The world no longer belongs to them.</i>

385
01:15:16.345 --> 01:15:19.265
<i>It belongs to another set of players.</i>

386
01:15:21.475 --> 01:15:23.227
<i>The creatures of darkness.</i>

387
01:16:54.860 --> 01:16:58.823
<i>The night can turn a friend
into a deadly foe.</i>

388
01:17:04.495 --> 01:17:05.621
<i>During the day,</i>

389
01:17:06.163 --> 01:17:11.293
<i>whitetip sharks are content
to cruise gently around the reef alone.</i>

390
01:17:20.386 --> 01:17:21.512
<i>But when night comes,</i>

391
01:17:23.139 --> 01:17:27.184
<i>they're transformed
into hunters working in packs.</i>

392
01:17:35.192 --> 01:17:37.403
<i>In the gloom,
the shark's eyesight is poor.</i>

393
01:17:41.073 --> 01:17:44.243
<i>But they can smell
potential prey from far off.</i>

394
01:17:48.164 --> 01:17:49.582
<i>And they have another advantage.</i>

395
01:17:50.583 --> 01:17:54.670
<i>A sixth sense, that can pick up
the tiny electrical signals</i>

396
01:17:55.087 --> 01:17:57.131
<i>from the heartbeat of a frightened fish.</i>

397
01:18:00.676 --> 01:18:01.844
<i>And track it down.</i>

398
01:18:08.309 --> 01:18:11.061
<i>Even the deepest shadow,
is no hiding place.</i>

399
01:19:01.028 --> 01:19:03.822
<i>Darkness is not just
a time for nightmares.</i>

400
01:19:05.658 --> 01:19:09.203
<i>But also for dreams and wonders.</i>

401
01:19:32.810 --> 01:19:36.563
<i>Energy stored
from the sunlight is recycled.</i>

402
01:19:38.941 --> 01:19:40.401
<i>And the world lights up again.</i>

403
01:20:05.092 --> 01:20:07.177
<i>Some creatures use their lights for love.</i>

404
01:20:12.349 --> 01:20:14.018
<i>For this male click beetle,</i>

405
01:20:14.435 --> 01:20:19.231
<i>his glowing spots are designed
to impress and attract a mate.</i>

406
01:20:22.484 --> 01:20:25.446
<i>And seeing the glow from this fungus,
he thinks he's found one...</i>

407
01:20:26.488 --> 01:20:27.489
<i>Hidden inside.</i>

408
01:20:33.495 --> 01:20:35.664
<i>But the fungus is playing a trick on him.</i>

409
01:20:36.498 --> 01:20:39.084
<i>The glow comes from the fungus itself.</i>

410
01:20:46.091 --> 01:20:47.801
<i>Puzzled, he searches everywhere.</i>

411
01:20:49.595 --> 01:20:51.930
<i>And gets covered in fungal spores.</i>

412
01:20:57.186 --> 01:20:59.480
<i>He'll spread them wherever he goes next.</i>

413
01:21:00.230 --> 01:21:05.694
<i>Not reproducing himself,
but helping reproduce the fungus instead.</i>

414
01:21:13.369 --> 01:21:17.289
<i>A light in the dark,
can also be a deadly trap.</i>

415
01:21:25.214 --> 01:21:28.842
<i>In New Zealand,
glow-worms cling to the roof of a cave.</i>

416
01:21:31.595 --> 01:21:35.766
<i>They shine out their strange lights
from within circles of hanging silk,</i>

417
01:21:36.433 --> 01:21:37.684
<i>sticky with mucus.</i>

418
01:21:47.736 --> 01:21:50.823
<i>Tiny flies are drawn
to the beautiful lights.</i>

419
01:21:52.574 --> 01:21:57.371
<i>Only to become glued
to the dangling strands and trapped.</i>

420
01:21:59.164 --> 01:22:01.542
<i>Later, they'll be reeled in for supper.</i>

421
01:22:17.641 --> 01:22:20.686
<i>And the night brings magic,
on a much grander scale.</i>

422
01:22:27.985 --> 01:22:30.195
<i>The sky seems to come alive.</i>

423
01:22:53.552 --> 01:22:57.055
<i>Even when the sun is out of sight,
it makes its presence felt.</i>

424
01:23:01.059 --> 01:23:05.105
<i>Its electrical energy powers a firework
display that lights up the planet.</i>

425
01:23:09.526 --> 01:23:10.527
<i>The Aurora.</i>

426
01:23:38.347 --> 01:23:40.265
<i>And there is another light show on earth.</i>

427
01:23:42.059 --> 01:23:43.560
<i>One powered by us.</i>

428
01:23:49.483 --> 01:23:51.610
<i>We no longer have to wait for sunrise.</i>

429
01:23:53.654 --> 01:23:56.073
<i>We no longer
need to be afraid of the dark.</i>

430
01:23:58.408 --> 01:24:01.870
<i>In our cities, we've created
an endless electrical daylight of our own.</i>

431
01:24:14.925 --> 01:24:17.553
<i>We've broken away
from the rhythm of night and day.</i>

432
01:24:28.730 --> 01:24:30.691
<i>As more and more of us live this way,</i>

433
01:24:30.774 --> 01:24:34.570
<i>it's easy for us to forget
our connexion to the natural world.</i>

434
01:24:36.154 --> 01:24:37.990
<i>Even, when it's on our doorstep.</i>

435
01:24:57.134 --> 01:25:01.221
<i>These raccoons in Toronto
seem just as home in the city, as we are.</i>

436
01:25:31.835 --> 01:25:34.463
<i>Not all creatures can adapt
so easily to our world.</i>

437
01:25:36.548 --> 01:25:38.467
<i>But we humans can do something to help.</i>

438
01:25:40.761 --> 01:25:44.473
<i>We have the ability to appreciate
what no other animal on earth can.</i>

439
01:25:47.476 --> 01:25:51.897
<i>If we open our eyes,
we can see the magic all around us.</i>

440
01:25:54.066 --> 01:25:56.568
<i>The extraordinary in the everyday.</i>

441
01:26:07.788 --> 01:26:12.084
<i>We can see the fragile web
that connects us with all living things.</i>

442
01:26:15.170 --> 01:26:17.923
<i>And understand that the future
of all life...</i>

443
01:26:18.882 --> 01:26:20.217
<i>Lies in our hands.</i>

444
01:26:40.570 --> 01:26:43.532
<i>We have searched
the far reaches of space for wonders.</i>

445
01:26:46.868 --> 01:26:51.164
<i>But instead, we found the most wonderful
things of all, back home.</i>

446
01:26:54.334 --> 01:26:56.461
<i>Here, on our lucky planet.</i>

447
01:26:58.296 --> 01:27:02.134
<i>Small and blue,
spinning in an ocean of stars.</i>

448
01:27:13.019 --> 01:27:15.188
<i>In the whole universe, as far as we know,</i>

449
01:27:16.940 --> 01:27:18.734
<i>there's nowhere else with life.</i>

450
01:27:20.110 --> 01:27:21.486
<i>Nothing more extraordinary...</i>

451
01:27:22.821 --> 01:27:23.864
<i>Than planet earth.</i>

452
01:27:25.574 --> 01:27:28.952
<i>Nothing more important to protect
than our one and only home.</i>

453
01:27:31.079 --> 01:27:36.793
<i>And nothing more amazing
than what happens here, day after day.</i>
